ata-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a class="hd__tel" href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>(508) 656-7436</a> <a class="btn hd__cta" href="/contact" data-ev="estimate_cta" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Free estimate</a> <button class="hd__burger" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mnav" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <span data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs></span><span data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs></span> </button> </div> </div> <nav class="mnav" id="mnav" hidden aria-label="Mobile" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a href="/kitchen-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Kitchen remodeling</a><a href="/bathroom-remodeling" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Bathroom remodeling</a><a href="/general-renovations" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>General renovations</a><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Carpentry</a><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Deck building</a><a href="/interior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Interior painting</a><a href="/exterior-painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Exterior painting</a><a href="/building-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Building restoration</a><a href="/water-damage-restoration" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Water damage restoration</a> <hr class="rule" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs> <a href="/painting" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Painting</a><a href="/portfolio" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Our work</a><a href="/areas-we-serve" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Areas we serve</a> <a href="/about" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>About</a><a href="/contact" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>Free estimate</a> <a class="mnav__tel" href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-nen7h5rs>(508) 656-7436</a> </div> </nav> </header> <script type="module">var e=document.querySelector(`.hd__burger`),t=document.getElementById(`mnav`);e?.addEventListener(`click`,()=>{let n=e.getAttribute(`aria-expanded`)===`true`;e.setAttribute(`aria-expanded`,String(!n)),t&&(t.hidden=n),e.setAttribute(`aria-label`,n?`Open menu`:`Close menu`)});</script> <main id="main" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <section class="top wrap-wide" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <div data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>/</span> <a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Decks</a></nav> <h1 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Multi-Level Decks and Pergolas</h1> <p class="cost" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Typical Central MA range: <strong data-astro-cid-j5amansv>$28,000–$60,000 per multi-level deck; pergola extra</strong></p> <p class="lead" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Two tiers down a sloped yard, an open-top pergola for shade, and built-in benches and planters.</p> <a class="btn" href="#estimate" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Book a free in-home consultation</a> </div> <figure data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <img src="/ideas/multi-level-decks-and-pergolas-main.webp" alt="Design idea: two-level composite deck stepping down a sloped backyard with an open-top wood pergola over the upper level" width="1600" height="1195" fetchpriority="high" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <figcaption data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Design idea (AI illustration) — not an MCB project photo.</figcaption> </figure> </section> <article class="wrap prose" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 id="who-this-kind-of-deck-is-for">Who this kind of deck is for</h2>
<p>Much of Central Massachusetts is not flat. Walkout basements, back doors six or eight feet above the lawn, ledge and old stone walls are normal in Holden, Sterling, Bolton and Westford. A single deck at door height on a lot like that becomes a platform on stilts. Breaking it into levels, and adding shade, seating and planting, turns it into an outdoor room.</p>
<p>This page goes into the design and build details. For a general overview see <a href="/deck-building">deck building</a>, and for how multi-level jobs compare on price, the <a href="/deck-building-cost-massachusetts">2026 deck cost guide</a>. Materials are covered on our <a href="/composite-deck-installers-central-ma">composite deck</a>, <a href="/deck-building/pvc-decks">PVC deck</a> and <a href="/deck-building/pressure-treated-decks">pressure-treated deck</a> pages.</p>
<h2 id="designing-for-a-grade-change">Designing for a grade change</h2>
<p><strong>Start with the doors and the lawn.</strong> The upper level sits just below the door threshold. The lower level goes where the yard is flattest or where you want to land: a patio, a fire pit, a view.</p>
<p><strong>Make the levels different jobs.</strong> A common layout puts grilling and a small table on the upper level near the kitchen, and lounge seating or a larger dining table below. A typical scope looks like a 12x14 upper level off the kitchen and a 16x18 lower level connected by a wide run of steps.</p>
<p><strong>Wide steps between levels.</strong> Three or four steps the full width of a section feel like part of the deck, not a staircase. They still follow the stair rules: equal risers, treads at least 10 inches deep in the model code, and a handrail once there are four or more risers.</p>
<p><strong>Guards level by level.</strong> Each level needs a guard wherever its surface is more than 30 inches above the grade below. A lower level kept under that height can often stay open, which keeps the view and saves money. Confirm heights and details with your local building department.</p>
<p><strong>Tall posts need bracing.</strong> Posts over about six feet get heavier sizing, bracing and careful beam connections. Footings for every level still go below frost depth, commonly 48 inches here, and each one is inspected.</p>
<p><strong>Low levels need air.</strong> A lower deck close to grade stays damp. We use ground-contact treated framing, keep a gap for airflow, and lay fabric and stone underneath to keep weeds down and water moving.</p>
<h2 id="open-top-pergolas">Open-top pergolas</h2>
<p>An open-top pergola gives filtered shade, a frame for lights or a climbing vine, and a sense of enclosure without closing anything in. The details that matter:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Posts go to footings.</strong> Pergola posts carry down through the deck to their own footings, or land on beams designed for the load. They’re never lagged to the side of a joist or set on the boards.</li>
<li><strong>Wind.</strong> Open slats still catch wind. Posts are braced with knee braces or rigid connections, and rafters are tied down with hardware.</li>
<li><strong>Shade by spacing.</strong> Closer rafters and a layer of purlins give more shade. Orient the top members east to west to block more midday sun.</li>
<li><strong>Materials.</strong> Pressure-treated pine (painted or stained), cedar for a natural look, PVC-wrapped posts for low upkeep, or powder-coated aluminum kits. Wood looks best on older colonials; aluminum suits a modern house.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="built-in-benches-and-planters">Built-in benches and planters</h2>
<p><strong>Benches</strong> save furniture and define edges. Keep them off the edge of a raised deck unless the guard behind them is built to height from the seat. A comfortable seat is roughly 17 to 19 inches high and 16 to 20 inches deep.</p>
<p><strong>Planters</strong> soften a big deck. Wet soil is heavy, so large planters sit over beams or get their own support. They’re lined, drained and held off the decking, and never built so soil touches the frame. Cedar or PVC boxes hold up better than pine.</p>
<h2 id="what-it-costs-in-central-ma">What it costs in Central MA</h2>
<p>These are typical ranges, not quotes:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Typical scope</th>
<th>Typical installed range</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Two-level deck, 400–600 sq ft total, composite, aluminum rail, connecting steps</td>
<td>$28,000–$60,000</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Height, the number of levels, stair runs and railing choice move a multi-level deck around inside that range. Pergolas, benches and planters are priced separately at the consultation. Low-voltage lighting and electrical work are quoted separately. Our written estimate itemises each level, the pergola, the built-ins, the exact materials and what’s excluded.</p>
<h2 id="what-the-job-involves">What the job involves</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Site visit and grades.</strong> We shoot elevations at the door, the far corners and the landing points, and look for ledge and old walls.</li>
<li><strong>Design and permit.</strong> A plan showing each level, stair runs, guards and the pergola goes to the building department.</li>
<li><strong>Footings.</strong> All levels and pergola posts, inspected before framing.</li>
<li><strong>Framing, level by level,</strong> from the top down or bottom up depending on access.</li>
<li><strong>Decking, steps, railings, then pergola and built-ins.</strong></li>
<li><strong>Final inspection and cleanup.</strong></li>
</ol>
<p>On-site work for a two-level deck with a pergola typically runs three to five weeks after the permit.</p>
<h2 id="new-england-issues">New England issues</h2>
<p><strong>Ledge and boulders.</strong> Holes in Northborough and Westford sometimes hit rock. Footings on ledge follow the engineer’s or inspector’s direction, and we price that possibility in the estimate.</p>
<p><strong>Snow.</strong> Pergolas shed snow; a solid top would not, which is one reason we build them open. Leave room to shovel steps between levels.</p>
<p><strong>Older houses.</strong> Where the upper level ties into a pre-1978 house, ask any contractor for their lead-safe certification in writing before siding or painted trim is disturbed.</p>
<h2 id="what-to-ask-any-contractor-about-a-multi-level-deck">What to ask any contractor about a multi-level deck</h2>
<ul>
<li>Where does each level sit relative to the door and the grade?</li>
<li>Which levels need guards, and why?</li>
<li>Where do the pergola posts land?</li>
<li>Are benches designed with guard height in mind?</li>
<li>How is rock or ledge priced if you hit it?</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="next-step">Next step</h2>
<p>We’ll come out for a free consultation: walk the slope, take elevations, bring samples, and follow up with a written estimate that itemises each level, the pergola, the built-ins and what’s excluded.</p>
 <section class="faq" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Common questions</h2> <details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Why build two levels instead of one big deck?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>On a sloped lot, a single deck at door height ends up high off the ground at the far end, with tall posts, a long stair and a guard all the way around. Stepping down to a second level closer to grade often means shorter posts, less railing and a space that feels connected to the yard.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Does a pergola on a deck need a permit?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Often, yes, because it&#39;s a structure that adds load and wind forces to the deck. Towns handle it differently, so we include it in the deck permit or file it separately as your building department requires.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Can a pergola be attached to my existing deck?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Only if the posts can carry down to proper footings. We don&#39;t bolt pergola posts to the deck boards or the side of a joist. On an existing deck that usually means opening the decking, adding footings below frost depth and running the posts down through the frame.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Can a built-in bench take the place of a railing?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Not by itself. If the deck is high enough to need a guard, a bench along the edge becomes something to stand on, and many inspectors measure guard height from the seat. We either build the guard at the right height behind the bench or keep benches away from the drop.</p></details><details data-astro-cid-j5amansv><summary data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Do built-in planters rot the deck?</summary><p data-astro-cid-j5amansv>They can if soil and water sit against the framing. We line planters, give them drainage, and hold them off the deck surface so water drains away and air can move underneath.</p></details> </section> </article> <section class="wrap-wide more" data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <h2 data-astro-cid-j5amansv>More deck ideas</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-j5amansv> <li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/deck-building/pressure-treated-decks" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/pressure-treated-decks-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of pressure-treated deck boards with face screws in a straight line over a joist" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Pressure-Treated Wood Decks</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/deck-building/pvc-decks" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/pvc-decks-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of grooved PVC deck boards with hidden fasteners and a picture-frame border" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>PVC Decks: AZEK and TimberTech Advanced PVC</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/deck-building/deck-railings-and-stairs" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/deck-railings-and-stairs-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of a black aluminum baluster railing meeting a white composite post with a solid rail cap" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Deck Railings and Stairs</span></a></li><li data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/deck-building/deck-repair-and-rebuilds" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><img src="/ideas/deck-repair-and-rebuilds-detail.webp" alt="Design idea: close-up of a deck ledger bolted to a house rim with metal flashing tucked behind the siding" width="800" height="800" loading="lazy" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><span data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Deck Repair and Rebuilds</span></a></li> </ul> <p data-astro-cid-j5amansv><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-j5amansv>Back to decks</a></p> </section> <div id="estimate" data-astro-cid-j5amansv><form class="ef" id="estimate-form" novalidate data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-name" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Name <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-name" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Please tell us your name.</p> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-phone" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Phone <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-phone" name="phone" type="tel" inputmode="tel" autocomplete="tel" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-phone" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>We need a phone number to reach you.</p> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-email" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Email</label> <input id="ef-email" name="email" type="email" inputmode="email" autocomplete="email" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-email" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>That email address doesn't look right.</p> </div> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-town" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project town <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <input id="ef-town" name="town" type="text" autocomplete="address-level2" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-town" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Which town is the project in?</p> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-type" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project type <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <select id="ef-type" name="projectType" required data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option value="" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Choose one…</option> <option value="Kitchen remodeling" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Kitchen remodeling</option><option value="Bathroom remodeling" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Bathroom remodeling</option><option value="General renovations" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>General renovations</option><option value="Carpentry" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Carpentry</option><option value="Deck building" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Deck building</option><option value="Interior painting" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Interior painting</option><option value="Exterior painting" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Exterior painting</option><option value="Building restoration" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Building restoration</option><option value="Water damage restoration" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Water damage restoration</option> <option value="Multiple / not sure" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Multiple, or not sure yet</option> </select> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-type" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Please pick the closest match.</p> </div> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-details" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Project details <abbr title="required" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>*</abbr></label> <textarea id="ef-details" name="projectDetails" rows="5" required placeholder="What you want done, roughly when, and anything you already know about the space." data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn></textarea> <p class="ef__err" data-err="ef-details" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>A sentence or two is plenty.</p> </div> <div class="ef__grid" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-timing" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Desired timing</label> <select id="ef-timing" name="timing" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option value="" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>No strong preference</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>As soon as possible</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Within 1–3 months</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Within 3–6 months</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Later this year</option> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Just planning / budgeting</option> </select> </div> <div class="ef__row" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-contact" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Preferred contact</label> <select id="ef-contact" name="preferredContact" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Phone call</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Text message</option><option data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Email</option> </select> </div> </div> <!-- Honeypot. Off-screen, aria-hidden, never focusable. --> <div class="ef__hp" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <label for="ef-company" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Company</label> <input id="ef-company" name="company" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> </div> <p class="ef__consent" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>
By sending this you agree we can contact you about your project by phone, text or email.
    Message rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out of texts at any time. We don't sell your details.
</p> <button class="btn ef__submit" type="submit" data-ev="form_submit" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Send it over</button> <p class="ef__note" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>We read every one of these. Prefer to talk?
<a href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>(508) 656-7436</a>.</p> <p class="ef__fail" id="ef-fail" role="alert" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn></p> </form> <div class="ef__ok" id="ef-ok" role="status" hidden data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn> <h3 data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Got it.</h3> <p data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>Your details are with us. We'll be in touch to arrange a look at the project.
     If it's urgent, call <a href="tel:+15086567436" data-astro-cid-xxufhcpn>(508) 656-7436</a>.</p> </div> <script>(function(){const CRM = {"endpoint":"https://backend.leadconnectorhq.com/external-tracking/events","locationId":"b5lmCvdlpVkhC4JOVBjd","trackingId":"tk_e76468050a3e42e0b65b2fa5b3c87a7f"};
const PHONE = "(508) 656-7436";
const EMAIL = "douglas@mcitybuilders.com";

  const form = document.getElementById('estimate-form');
  const okBox = document.getElementById('ef-ok');
  const failBox = document.getElementById('ef-fail');
  if (form) {
    const started = Date.now();
    let announcedStart = false;
    form.addEventListener('input', () => {
      if (!announcedStart && typeof gtag === 'function') {
        announcedStart = true;
        gtag('event', 'form_start', { form_id: 'mcb_estimate' });   // no field contents
      }
    }, { once: false });

    const showErr = (el, on) => {
      el.setAttribute('aria-invalid', String(on));
      const p = form.querySelector('[data-err="' + el.id + '"]');
      if (p) p.hidden = !on;
    };

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      failBox.hidden = true;

      // --- validation with real messages, focus moved to the first problem
      let firstBad = null;
      for (const el of form.querySelectorAll('[required]')) {
        const bad = !el.value.trim();
        showErr(el, bad);
        if (bad && !firstBad) firstBad = el;
      }
      const em = form.querySelector('#ef-email');
      const emBad = em.value.trim() !== '' && !/^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]{2,}$/.test(em.value.trim());
      showErr(em, emBad);
      if (emBad && !firstBad) firstBad = em;
      if (firstBad) { firstBad.focus(); return; }

      // --- bot gates: hidden field filled, or submitted faster than a human types
      const fd = new FormData(form);
      if (String(fd.get('company') || '').trim() !== '' || Date.now() - started < 3000) {
        form.hidden = true; okBox.hidden = false; return;   // silent, nothing sent
      }

      const btn = form.querySelector('.ef__submit');
      const label = btn.textContent;
      btn.textContent = 'Sending…'; btn.disabled = true;

      let ss = null; try { ss = sessionStorage; } catch (_) {}
      const attr = (k) => { try { return (ss && ss.getItem('mcb_' + k)) || ''; } catch (_) { return ''; } };

      const payload = {
        type: 'external_form_submission',
        timestamp: Date.now(),
        formId: 'Estimate Request',
        formData: {
          full_name: fd.get('name'),
          phone: fd.get('phone'),
          email: fd.get('email') || '',          // logical OR. Not a pipe.
          'contact.project_details': fd.get('projectDetails'),
          project_town: fd.get('town'),
          project_type: fd.get('projectType'),
          timing: fd.get('timing') || '',
          preferred_contact: fd.get('preferredContact') || '',
          utm_source: attr('utm_source'), utm_medium: attr('utm_medium'),
          utm_campaign: attr('utm_campaign'), utm_term: attr('utm_term'),
          utm_content: attr('utm_content'), gclid: attr('gclid'), fbclid: attr('fbclid'),
          landing_page: attr('mcb_landing') || attr('landing'),
          referrer: attr('referrer') || document.referrer || '',
          Timezone: Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone,
        },
        url: location.href, title: document.title, path: location.pathname,
        userAgent: navigator.userAgent,
        trackingId: CRM.trackingId, locationId: CRM.locationId,
        sessionId: (crypto && crypto.randomUUID) ? crypto.randomUUID() : String(Math.random()).slice(2),
      };

      let ok = false, diag = '';
      try {
        const res = await fetch(CRM.endpoint, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', version: '2021-07-28' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        });
        ok = res.ok; diag = 'HTTP ' + res.status;
      } catch (err) { diag = 'network: ' + (err && err.message); }

      if (!ok) {
        // Nothing reached the CRM. Keep every keystroke on screen, give a real
        // route through, and do NOT report a conversion.
        console.error('[MCB estimate form]', diag);
        btn.textContent = label; btn.disabled = false;
        failBox.innerHTML = 'We couldn\'t send that from the website. Please call ' +
          '<a href="tel:+15086567436">' + PHONE + '</a> or email ' +
          '<a href="mailto:' + EMAIL + '">' + EMAIL + '</a>. ' +
          'Everything you typed is still in the form above.';
        failBox.hidden = false;
        failBox.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
        return;
      }

      if (typeof gtag === 'function') {
        gtag('event', 'generate_lead', { form_id: 'mcb_estimate', lead_source: 'website_estimate_form' });
      }
      form.hidden = true; okBox.hidden = false;
      okBox.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      okBox.querySelector('h3').setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
      okBox.querySelector('h3').focus();
    });
  }
})();</script></div> </main> <footer class="ft" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="wrap" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="ft__top" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <span class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Maverick City Builders</span> <p class="ft__pitch" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>General contracting and remodeling across Massachusetts.</p> <a class="btn btn--onDark" href="/contact" data-ev="estimate_cta" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Request an estimate</a> </div> <nav aria-label="Services" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Services</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/kitchen-remodeling" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Kitchen remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/bathroom-remodeling" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Bathroom remodeling</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/general-renovations" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>General renovations</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/carpentry" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Carpentry</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/deck-building" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Deck building</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/interior-painting" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Interior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/exterior-painting" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Exterior painting</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/building-restoration" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Building restoration</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/water-damage-restoration" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Water damage restoration</a></li></ul> </nav> <nav aria-label="Company" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Company</h2> <ul data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/about" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>About</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/portfolio" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Our work</a></li> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/areas-we-serve" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Areas we serve</a></li><li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/blog" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Articles</a></li> <li data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/contact" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Contact</a></li> </ul> </nav> <div data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><h2 class="ft__h" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Contact</h2> <address class="ft__nap" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <a href="tel:+15086567436" data-ev="phone_click" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>(508) 656-7436</a> <a href="mailto:douglas@mcitybuilders.com" data-ev="email_click" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>douglas@mcitybuilders.com</a> <span data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>1171 Main St<br data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Lancaster, MA 01523</span> <em data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Office visits by appointment</em> </address> </div> </div> <hr class="rule" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <div class="ft__base" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk> <p data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>&copy; 2026 Maverick City Builders &middot; Lancaster, Massachusetts</p> <p data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk><a href="/privacy-policy" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Privacy</a> &middot; <a href="/terms" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Terms</a> &middot;
<a href="/accessibility" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Accessibility</a> &middot; <a href="/cookie-policy" data-astro-cid-jo6i4kqk>Cookies</a></p> </div> </div> </footer> </main>  <div id="mcb-cookie-banner" hidden role="dialog" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Cookie choices" style="position:fixed;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:99999;background:#0b0b0b;border-top:2px solid #E10600;color:#e6e6e6;padding:18px 20px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;align-items:center;justify-content:center"> <span style="max-width:640px">We measure page views with Google Analytics in cookieless mode. Accept to allow analytics cookies and ad measurement; Decline to stay cookieless. Read our <a href="/cookie-policy" style="color:#ff6b6b;text-decoration:underline">Cookie Policy</a>.</span> <span style="display:flex;gap:10px"> <button type="button" id="mcb-cookie-decline" style="background:transparent;color:#e6e6e6;border:1px solid #777;padding:12px 20px;min-height:44px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">Decline</button> <button type="button" id="mcb-cookie-accept" style="background:#E10600;color:#fff;border:0;padding:12px 22px;min-height:44px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">Accept</button> </span> </div> <!-- Analytics with Google Consent Mode (mcb-consent-v2, 2026-09-18, Doug's decision).
       GA4 loads by default with analytics_storage DENIED = cookieless pings, no _ga cookie.
       Accept upgrades consent to granted. Browsers sending Do-Not-Track or Global Privacy
       Control get nothing at all. The static site does the same via patch_consent.py. --> <script>(function(){const ga4 = "G-7HXJQJL5Q2";

    (function () {
      var KEY = 'mcb-consent'; // MUST match the static site's key (hyphen). An underscore here meant GA4 never loaded on any Astro page.
      var dnt = false;
      try { dnt = navigator.doNotTrack == '1' || window.doNotTrack == '1' || !!navigator.globalPrivacyControl; } catch (e) {}
      window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
      window.gtag = function () { window.dataLayer.push(arguments); };
      gtag('consent', 'default', { ad_storage: 'denied', ad_user_data: 'denied', ad_personalization: 'denied',
        analytics_storage: 'denied', functionality_storage: 'granted', security_storage: 'granted' });
      function load() {
        if (window.__mcbTagged) return; window.__mcbTagged = true;
        var s = document.createElement('script'); s.async = true;
        s.src = 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=' + ga4;
        document.head.appendChild(s);
        gtag('js', new Date()); gtag('config', ga4);
      }
      function boot() { // Accept: cookies + ad measurement allowed
        gtag('consent', 'update', { ad_storage: 'granted', ad_user_data: 'granted', ad_personalization: 'granted', analytics_storage: 'granted' });
        load();
      }
      var stored = null;
      try { stored = localStorage.getItem(KEY); } catch (e) {}
      if (stored === 'granted') boot();
      else if (!dnt) load(); // undecided or declined: cookieless measurement only
      window.__mcbConsentBoot = boot;
      // Same banner as the static site. Without it a visitor who LANDS on a town page
      // is never asked, so is never measured.
      try {
        var v = localStorage.getItem(KEY), b = document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-banner');
        if (b && v !== 'granted' && v !== 'denied') {
          b.hidden = false;
          document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-accept').addEventListener('click', function () { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, 'granted'); } catch (e) {} b.hidden = true; boot(); });
          document.getElementById('mcb-cookie-decline').addEventListener('click', function () { try { localStorage.setItem(KEY, 'denied'); } catch (e) {} b.hidden = true; });
        }
      } catch (e) {}
      // lightweight, non-sensitive interaction events
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var a = e.target && e.target.closest && e.target.closest('[data-ev]');
        if (a && typeof window.gtag === 'function') {
          gtag('event', a.getAttribute('data-ev'), { link_url: a.getAttribute('href') || '' });
        }
      }, true);
    })();
  })();</script></body> </html>